{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game","id":1378946,"title":"Onyx Path should do a steampunk game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-06T00:30:11-07:00","id":1378946,"title":"Onyx Path should do a steampunk game.","content":"Industrial fantasy, magic punk, steam punk, any of these would be really cool I think. Anyone one else think this would be fun? I'm actually kind of surprised they don't already have something like this. All their games are niche genres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T08:48:10-07:00","id":1378996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game#post1378946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Industrial fantasy, magic punk, steam punk, any of these would be really cool I think. Anyone one else think this would be fun? I'm actually kind of surprised they don't already have something like this. All their games are niche genres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t see any reason not to use the already existing framework of Trinity Continuum via a Steampunk era/setting book.<br /> <br /> Of course I\u2019ll be over here arguing that to really stand out in the genre, they should actually deliver the \u201cpunk\u201d factor, aggressively reject imperial fetishism, and play up that it\u2019s the lower class and colonized demos who are jerryrigging the iconic clockwork tech from the scraps they get access to, and how if the East India Company isn\u2019t a GIANT EVIL MEGACORP than nothing is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T10:36:01-07:00","id":1379018,"title":"","content":"Do not have we already as <b>TC</b> 'subgame' pitch? <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contorting-your-continuum-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Contorting Your Continuum</b></a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Contorting Your Contunuum blog</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>December 13, 1795: EXTRAORDINARY STONE Falls from Atmosphere \u2013 Lands at Wold Newton Cottage. Proof of Existence of Extra-Terrestrial Matter?</i> <hr /> My goal with the <b>Trinity Continuum</b> \u2014 at least, the core setting \u2014 was to set up a sort of \u201cLeague of Extraordinary Gentlemen\u201d setting: a setting where all works of fiction (or at least, the non-magical ones) co-exist. There\u2019s a lot of ways you can approach this, based on the needs of your own game. <hr /> <i>August 3, 1997: Cyber Division of Einsystems, Inc. set to launch Global Defense Digital Network. Project Lead Dyson: \u201cVery Pleased\u201d</i> <hr /> <b>Using the above examples, perhaps in your game you\u2019re playing</b><br /> Les Fant\u00f4mes because you like the heist genre, using our provided Allegiance for playing the sort of game you like to play. Alternately, you could use the Ghosts as a basis for portraying a member of Leverage, International, or perhaps one of Danny Ocean\u2019s associates, removing a layer of abstraction and going right to the source material. Or you could work on a combination approach: Les Fant\u00f4mes and Leverage and the Oceans exist in the same universe. Sometimes they work together. Sometimes they\u2019re at odds (something like the Leverage episode \u201cThe Two Live Crew Job\u201d). <hr /> <i>October 9, 2016: From the Desk of Maxwell Mercer: Stay out of Riverport!!! until at least five years have passed.</i> <hr /> Similarly, perhaps your team of specialists was assembled by the mysterious Pharos. Or perhaps it was Charlie, or Miranda Zero, or the Machine. Or, interestingly, perhaps some or all of the above characters are actually the same. If the Machine is secretly Pharos, why is it hiding its activity separately from Finch\u2019s team? Does Nathan Drake work with the Global Cartography Initiative, or are the GCI working with Katherine Marlowe? <hr /> <i>Report, December 21, 1979: There\u2019s been another sighting of one of the five alleged \u201cHollywood Wizards.\u201d Experts examining the footage are still unsure if he\u2019s actually that fast, or it\u2019s just an elaborate special effect.</i> <hr /> We tried to use our framework to give you as many options as possible to play the sorts of games you want to play, but also to provide some pretty compelling stories. You can use different Allegiances as antagonists to each other, different factions within a single Allegiance, or two separate-but-similar Allegiances who are both racing to reach the same McGuffin.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a big Continuum, and anything and everything you find enjoyable can and should be a part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-06-2020, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T15:38:53-07:00","id":1379079,"title":"","content":"What about like a Trinity version of Castle Falkenstein? I never played the original game, but I\u2019ve heard it\u2019s pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:31:45-07:00","id":1379121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1379079#post1379079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about like a Trinity version of Castle Falkenstein? I never played the original game, but I\u2019ve heard it\u2019s pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caltle Falkenstein is a great game, the setting is awesome, but the system is... unusual. I didn\u2019t get it when I was younger, now I am just lazy to try again.<br /> <br /> Yet, it\u2019s fairly easy to adapt it to TC. Just make a couple of templates for the races and treat magical items as super tech. I don\u2019t recal how powerful the magic in the setting is, but as far as I recall it\u2019s more Steam Punk than fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:35:46-07:00","id":1379123,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz cool. I just checked it out on DTRPG. I like 7th Sea better, but if you want a Victorian adventure game it sounds ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T22:11:49-07:00","id":1379177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1378996#post1378996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t see any reason not to use the already existing framework of Trinity Continuum via a Steampunk era/setting book.<br /> <br /> Of course I\u2019ll be over here arguing that to really stand out in the genre, they should actually deliver the \u201cpunk\u201d factor, aggressively reject imperial fetishism, and play up that it\u2019s the lower class and colonized demos who are jerryrigging the iconic clockwork tech from the scraps they get access to, and how if the East India Company isn\u2019t a GIANT EVIL MEGACORP than nothing is!</div> </div> </div> </div>The social tropes isnt really what I meant. I'm talking about airships, magical fuel crystals, golems, and inventors. Basically fantasy technology. If you used Trinity Core to make your own steampunk setting you would have to do a ton of work making inventions and stuff. I wouldn't want to flesh out a world by needing to use their super science rules it would just take too long. If they made a book to hang off of Trinity that would be cool cause then you could just slightly tweak the setting and use all the gear and abilities from the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T23:25:25-07:00","id":1379182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1379177#post1379177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The social tropes isnt really what I meant. I'm talking about airships, magical fuel crystals, golems, and inventors. Basically fantasy technology. If you used Trinity Core to make your own steampunk setting you would have to do a ton of work making inventions and stuff. I wouldn't want to flesh out a world by needing to use their super science rules it would just take too long. If they made a book to hang off of Trinity that would be cool cause then you could just slightly tweak the setting and use all the gear and abilities from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> hence my saying it should be an era for Trinity Continuum, I wasn\u2019t saying \u201cTrinity Continuum has already done all the work for you\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T06:18:44-07:00","id":1379469,"title":"","content":"*looks up from reading &quot;Arsene Lupin vs Herlock Sholmes&quot;*<br /> <br /> Huh? A steampunk game? Interesting...<br /> <br /> *goes back to reading*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T04:32:57-07:00","id":1379728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1379079#post1379079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about like a Trinity version of Castle Falkenstein? I never played the original game, but I\u2019ve heard it\u2019s pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Falkenstein was a fun setting, though the system was very 90s. However, its Steam-Age, Lost Notebooks of Leonardo DeVinci, and Comme il Faut (the book of manners and high society) are still some of my favorites from that decade. (I think there is a recent licensed sourcebook, Variations on the Great Game, that offers a bunch of alternative rule systems.)<br /> <br /> I've long wanted to try to make a mid-19th century steam-fantasy inspired setting to use for a Pathfinder 1st ed game, but haven't really had a group to try it with. <br /> <br /> If I were to try to create that sort of setting, I'd likely take a page from Robert E. Howard's Conan stories and Green Ronin's Damnation Decade setting, in which it's a fictional world that is clearly analogous to ours with place names that are meant to be recognizable shorthand for what they're meant to represent, but because it's fictional not-Earth, there's only as much historical baggage as one wishes to include. I'd also probably heavily Balkanize everything, breaking everything up into smaller nations that more strongly reflect their regional character and aspects of the setting or different genres. The &quot;US&quot; east of the Mississippi being broken up into Deep South, Appalachian, Tidewater, Midwest, Mid-Atlantic, and New England regions; Britain broken up into Scottish Highlands, Lowlands, the North, the Midlands, the South, Wales, and Cornwall; France into Brittany, Burgundy, Province, etc; and so on. Also a lot of pastiches of famous fictional characters instead of the actual characters themselves, so that the PCs can't just presume that the Holmes stand in is necessarily the good guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:32:36-07:00","id":1379799,"title":"","content":"I like pastiche characters. Edith Wharton is a really good author as far as getting a feel for Victorian-era culture and mores, but not a lot of gaming-related stuff happens in her novels (The Age of Innocence is all about a guy\u2019s internal agony over whether he should pursue his True Love over society\u2019s objections or just marry the woman he\u2019s supposed to marry instead).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:07:44-07:00","id":1379814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1379799#post1379799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like pastiche characters. Edith Wharton is a really good author as far as getting a feel for Victorian-era culture and mores, but not a lot of gaming-related stuff happens in her novels (The Age of Innocence is all about a guy\u2019s internal agony over whether he should pursue his True Love over society\u2019s objections or just marry the woman he\u2019s supposed to marry instead).</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend Anne Perry's mystery novels. They touch on a huge swath of Victorian British culture, especially as to how class and gender color peoples' perceptions, and do a wonderful job of showing what women in the period could and did do in spite of societal restrictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T11:40:29-07:00","id":1379820,"title":"","content":"Awesome \ud83d\ude0a. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:19:54-07:00","id":1379922,"title":"","content":"I would love to see a film noir-style oilpunk game with blimps and mutants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:38:48-07:00","id":1379966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1379121#post1379121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Caltle Falkenstein is a great game, the setting is awesome, but the system is... unusual. I didn\u2019t get it when I was younger, now I am just lazy to try again.<br /> <br /> Yet, it\u2019s fairly easy to adapt it to TC. Just make a couple of templates for the races and treat magical items as super tech. I don\u2019t recal how powerful the magic in the setting is, but as far as I recall it\u2019s more Steam Punk than fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Castle Falkenstein is what I point to whenever anyone asks me what <b>Mage: the Victorian Age</b> will look like. More or less. Yes,it is at its root a steampunk setting. But it also has magic, faeries, dragons, and its own variety of technomagic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:40:39-07:00","id":1379990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1379966#post1379966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castle Falkenstein is what I point to whenever anyone asks me what <b>Mage: the Victorian Age</b> will look like. More or less. Yes,it is at its root a steampunk setting. But it also has magic, faeries, dragons, and its own variety of technomagic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember all the elements of magic setting, but can\u2019t remember if the magic is DnD-ish or less powerful. I mean, the dwarfs are pretty much inventors, they use steam technology with some magic and there are sorcerers, but how dependent on magic is the society? How powerful are the sorcerers? They cast magic for everything or are more dependent on rituals? Things like that that I dont remenber. <br /> <br /> you answered it, it\u2019s DnD level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T21:24:04-07:00","id":1380026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1379922#post1379922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to see a film noir-style oilpunk game with blimps and mutants.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would be the general tropes of oilpunk? Also the general timeframe? (Cyberpunk is largely associated stylisticly and thematically with what was going on in the late 70s and early 80s, for example.)<br /> <br /> Also a topic for discussion: What would places like Brazil or Egypt or Persia look like in a steampunk setting? These things tend to focus on England, Western or Central Europe, or the Wild West (and Japan, usually in anime), but I never really see other areas developed or described much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 04-10-2020, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T05:14:02-07:00","id":1380089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380026#post1380026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a topic for discussion: What would places like Brazil or Egypt or Persia look like in a steampunk setting? These things tend to focus on England, Western or Central Europe, or the Wild West (and Japan, usually in anime), but I never really see other areas developed or described much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those places are the places that are explored by the adventurers, and so are more savage than steamy. I would make the main cities looking a lot like their European counterpart, but the rest would be almost empty of human population, much like Wild West, with a few villages here and there where you can find supply and guides (and other adventurers).<br /> If you have some fantasy elements the main reason to have so little people is the magical creatures, otherwise it\u2019s just because there are not many people living outside the main cities (like today, but with 2 billion people instead of 7).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:33:45-07:00","id":1380110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380026#post1380026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would be the general tropes of oilpunk? Also the general timeframe? (Cyberpunk is largely associated stylisticly and thematically with what was going on in the late 70s and early 80s, for example.)<br /> <br /> Also a topic for discussion: What would places like Brazil or Egypt or Persia look like in a steampunk setting? These things tend to focus on England, Western or Central Europe, or the Wild West (and Japan, usually in anime), but I never really see other areas developed or described much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The picture I have in my head is 1940s style film noir with cigar-smoking whiskey-drinking detectives or deadly poison-tongued femme fatales. Dark and disturbing machinery and tall black coal-burning factories covering the skies with dark clouds. Evil experiments using oil as a super fuel and incorporates it into human beings, turning them into mutants drooping black ichor. A lot of rain and smoky black fog. Low saturation and internal monologues. Could be a neat setting for a Chronicles of Darkness game too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:49:44-07:00","id":1380113,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the reasons I mention places like that is that, while steampunk tends to focus on Britain or the Wild West, I think that there's a lot more going on during the century that can be played with. Brazil, for example, depending on what part of the century you set it in, is either the Empire of Brazil or the First Republic. With the former, you have a fairly stable and economically strong constitutional monarchy, viewed as a very clear regional power and a possible growing international one, that works really well with some of the not so dark &quot;steam fantasy&quot; elements of something like Castle Faulkenstein, IMO. If the latter, you have a nominally democratic oligarchy with a growing urban population and industrialization that plays in to a lot of the same classic darker steampunk tropes as Britain or parts of the United States. <br /> Also, if I was trying to do a steampunk setting, one of the things I'd be interested in doing was mimicking what Aeon did, where you have these regions like South America, Africa and Australia taking a much larger and different role than they usually do in science fiction settings. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T10:09:47-07:00","id":1380154,"title":"","content":"I think we can balance the 2 parts and have a nice setting with explorers and developed areas in the same space.<br /> <br /> The same way USA had big cities in the east coast and a huge unexplored space in the middle, Brazil was a vast empty place for a long time. The area of Brazil is very close to the area of continuous USA (no Alaska and oceanic islands), and we have a huge forest that is hard to tame and explore, as a good part of it floods in the rain season (and Amazon river has 2 rain seasons, one from the north margin and one from the south margin, as its parallel to the equator and have the summer com each side as raining season).<br /> <br /> Even today that\u2019s are Indians living with no contact to modern civilization due to their location. Sure we had a pretty good grow in the end of empire, we probably had one of the best emperors in history, and as I said, big cities as Rio de Janeiro would be as active and technological as London and Paris, as it was probably about half a million people, but prior the massive immigration by the end of 1800 beginning of 1900, the population was very sparse. S\u00e3o Paulo was about half of the size of Rio back then, just because there was little to no immigrants (Sao Paulo is about 2 times bigger than Rio now, about 25million), half of the old city center (what we call old here) was build during and after First World War, so prior that Sao Paulo was quite small, more like a train hub than a city for it self, as it is the last stop before climbing down the Serra do Mar to reach the port of Santos (that, by the way was bigger than S\u00e3o Paulo back then).<br /> <br /> The northeast had several cities that would be great places to work with. They had people from several nationalities, as the empire opened the ports to receive foreigners, and would have the newest technology that could be transported. If there were steam zepelins they would stop there before going to Rio de Janeiro, Argentina and Chile, when coming from Europe (as they did later in real life).<br /> <br /> Yet, after a few hundred kilometer from the coast, it would be a great place for explorers, S\u00e3o Paulo state was the one that went deeper into the continent, creating villages that would become towns, but the rest of the country were almost completely savage. Marshal Rondon (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C\u00e2ndido_Rondon\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C\u00e2ndido_Rondon</a>) explored and mapped much of the western parts of Brazil in the 1910s to 1930s, so before that, while there were people living there, it was so isolated that they didn\u2019t even had an official map or the villages, not even the Army or the Government, there were even some forts that were build by the Portuguese to protect the borders and latter were abandoned (some forgotten almost completely).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T18:54:12-07:00","id":1380261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1379177#post1379177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The social tropes isnt really what I meant. I'm talking about airships, magical fuel crystals, golems, and inventors. Basically fantasy technology. If you used Trinity Core to make your own steampunk setting you would have to do a ton of work making inventions and stuff. I wouldn't want to flesh out a world by needing to use their super science rules it would just take too long. If they made a book to hang off of Trinity that would be cool cause then you could just slightly tweak the setting and use all the gear and abilities from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The social tropes are what make anything &quot;-punk&quot;. If you don't want that, then you want a Steam Fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T08:11:21-07:00","id":1380384,"title":"","content":"Technically true. In practice, \u201cSteampunk\u201d (and X-punk in general) has tended to focus on the technological side of things in a lot of peoples' imagination. I'll grant that it's not technically accurate; but that's still how to term tends to be used, accurate or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T08:58:47-07:00","id":1380388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380026#post1380026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a topic for discussion: What would places like Brazil or Egypt or Persia look like in a steampunk setting? These things tend to focus on England, Western or Central Europe, or the Wild West (and Japan, usually in anime), but I never really see other areas developed or described much.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game &quot;80 days&quot; is amazing for detailing an alternate steampunk 1872 using all kinds of cultures of the World and their tales and variations of steampunk technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T09:31:45-07:00","id":1380392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380384#post1380384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically true. In practice, \u201cSteampunk\u201d (and X-punk in general) has tended to focus on the technological side of things in a lot of peoples' imagination. I'll grant that it's not technically accurate; but that's still how to term tends to be used, accurate or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal preference is the term Steamtech for the technology aspect, and Victoriana for the time period tropes (alternatively Regency, Belle Epoque or others). Then Steampunk or Steamromance to express certain sociopolitical presumptions, Steamfantasy if it involves magic or fairies and the like, Steamhorror if incorporating monsters or Mythos type things, etc. But I am sometimes needlessly pedantic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T09:51:11-07:00","id":1380398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380384#post1380384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically true. In practice, \u201cSteampunk\u201d (and X-punk in general) has tended to focus on the technological side of things in a lot of peoples' imagination. I'll grant that it's not technically accurate; but that's still how to term tends to be used, accurate or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>In practice, Steampunk is a meaningless word thrown around by a comfortable majority looking for excuse to swageer in the attire and thoughts of a overly romanticized time while still feeling like they're sticking it to their parents.<br /> <br /> I'm quite done with that and want my punk fiction to <i>actually be punk</i>. Not the mayopunk I've been seeing churned out in the last decade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-11-2020, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:14:43-07:00","id":1380411,"title":"","content":"What I understand as \u201c-Punk\u201d is what the Punk movement fight against, that is basically a system where people have less value than what they produce in general. So Steam-Punk is about people having less value than technology, but with steam tech involved, diesel-punk is about people having less value than technology, but with diesel tech, cyberpunk same thing, but with cybernetics. Punk Gothic (the original VtM setting) was about people having no value while the city is big and oppressive due to the religious architecture (some buildings treat business as religion for that end) and presence of monsters.<br /> <br /> Castle Falkentein is definitely Steam Fantasy, and have little to no punk aspect on it, as it\u2019s about important people doing important stuff to the population in general. Shadow run is Fantasy-Cyber-Punk as people are marginalized by the corporations and technology and magic.<br /> <br /> But I agree that the idea of -punk is usually used to make it sounds rebellious, while it is usually not at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:04:33-07:00","id":1380473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380411#post1380411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Punk Gothic (the original VtM setting) was about people having no value while the city is big and oppressive due to the religious architecture (some buildings treat business as religion for that end) and presence of monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. There was an article in White Wolf Magazine around 25 years ago that actually went to the trouble of explaining what &quot;Gothic Punk&quot; was supposed to mean, and I rather wish something along those lines had been included in the revised edition core books (or even the 20th anniversary ones).<br /> The Gothic part refers to the Gothic literary genre of the 18th and 19th centuries, as well as its various decedents and spin offs (Southern Gothic, German &quot;Shudder Novels&quot;, Pulp Horror, Hammer horror films, etc.), as well as to the late medieval architecture, especially symbols of authority such as castles and cathedrals, which played a big part in it. This combination of age, size, and power over people gives off a mood of oppression and of the protagonist's inherent weakness in the greater scheme of the world. Likewise, the literature has a recurring theme of the protagonist being at a severe disadvantage against various oppressive forces from both the past and the present. <br /> The Punk part has less to do with the broad (and rather disorganized and widely varied) music scene of the 1970s (or with its stylistic look) and more with a lot of the attitudes that drove it. Namely, <i>Be yourself and fuck anyone who has a problem with it</i>. It's about being a person and an individual rather than just a number or a cog. You - yes, <i>you</i> - are important and your voice is worth being heard, provided you are willing to speak up and accept the consequences that come with not going along with the crowd. It's not a particularly new phenomenon, existing in some way, shape, or form for much of human history. &quot;Punk&quot; is just a convenient label to put on it. <br /> So when you combine the two, you have a setting where the primary theme is of the weight of the past and the vast impersonal powers of the present are constantly bearing down oppressively on the world and those in it, contrasted with the primary mood of the protagonists rebelling against the status quo of banality, surrender, and ignorance. The dignity and dreams of the individual must constantly strive against the uncaring and corrupt forces that want to crush such things. <br /> (I actually hold up things like the Harry Potter novels, the Luke Cage series from Netflix, and the movie Frozen as decent examples of Gothic Punk, in which the main characters are all haunted by past events and constrained by present circumstances, but continue to strive against those things in the hope of something better. They just tend to have better weather and lighting than the World of Darkness.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:35:08-07:00","id":1380678,"title":"","content":"Honest question -<b> If you would do Steampunk Trinity Continuum era, what would be Aeon Society connection?</b> Aeon Soc. is created in 1920s, if I remember correctly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:25:36-07:00","id":1380696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380678#post1380678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honest question -<b> If you would do Steampunk Trinity Continuum era, what would be Aeon Society connection?</b> Aeon Soc. is created in 1920s, if I remember correctly...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Interesting question. I think part of it would depend on exactly how Mercer's powers work and what their limits are. If it's possible for him to travel to any period - or alternate continuity - in which a Flux type event has happened, then it's not inconceivable that at some point he showed up and established a version of Aeon. Alternately, if he can't do that, then it's possible that there might have been some sort of &quot;lost&quot; organization that predated Aeon, one that Mercer or others might have had family ties with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:12:28-07:00","id":1380731,"title":"","content":"I don't think the focus of Trinity Continuum is Aeon (altho it's on the 3 main and original settings), I think the name Trinity could be used to point the 3 sources of power (it was not, but definitely could be...).<br /> <br /> But as you asked, I would expand it to another Allegiance: Pharos is probably around because there are references to his presence since the 1800s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T19:15:44-07:00","id":1380825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380678#post1380678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honest question -<b> If you would do Steampunk Trinity Continuum era, what would be Aeon Society connection?</b> Aeon Soc. is created in 1920s, if I remember correctly...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380696#post1380696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Interesting question. I think part of it would depend on exactly how Mercer's powers work and what their limits are. If it's possible for him to travel to any period - or alternate continuity - in which a Flux type event has happened, then it's not inconceivable that at some point he showed up and established a version of Aeon. Alternately, if he can't do that, then it's possible that there might have been some sort of &quot;lost&quot; organization that predated Aeon, one that Mercer or others might have had family ties with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe in Steampunk Era there was something like first shot on to what would become stable Aeon Soc. in 1920s? You know, 'failed experiment'? It's basically idea of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_League_of_Extraordinary_Gentlemen\" target=\"_blank\">Leauge of Extraordinary Gentelmen of Alan Moore</a>, that is predecessor to modern Justice League.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T21:03:30-07:00","id":1381205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380678#post1380678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honest question -<b> If you would do Steampunk Trinity Continuum era, what would be Aeon Society connection?</b> Aeon Soc. is created in 1920s, if I remember correctly...</div> </div> </div> </div>As one of the settings we know that they\u2019d like to do is Ancient Greece, I don\u2019t think \u201cthe Aeon Society needs to exist\u201d is a requisite for a Trinity era.<br /> <br /> That said, Max is a time traveller, so him creating retroactive predecessor groups could happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T07:15:56-07:00","id":1381311,"title":"","content":"I'm currently poking at ideas for a mid-19th century Steam Fantasy setting I'm referring to as Perfidious Albion. Generally, I've split the island of Britain - or in this word Albion - into a number of rival kingdoms who are all in a perpetual state of rivalry/Cold War that plays itself out in a Great Game of political, economic and social intrigue. There is magic in this setting, but it's kind of a low key sort of thing. There are fey folk, but I'm not sure what sort of form they'll take. There may be vampires, I'm not sure yet. Visually, it looks very much like an anime. <br /> I only really have two kingdoms conceptually developed. The fist of the Kingdom of Gloriana, which is basically London/the Home Counties, the Southeast and East England areas. It's a Constitutional Monarchy traditionally ruled by a Queen as far back as the rebellion against the Caesarean Empire millennia ago. Visually it's very brass &amp; leather steam tech mixed with Victorian romance, though there is a class structure and all that. The urban areas are fairly high tech while the rural parts are fairly Hobbit Shire like. Its matriarchal traditions involve a certain level of gender equality. Generally a &quot;green and pleasant land&quot;. <br /> The the other one, to the north of Gloriana, is the Workers' Republic of Mercia, encompassing the Midlands and the souther parts of the North West. This nation is a lot more steam punk, its current government the result of a workers' revolt about a century ago. It's highly industrialized, a bit Dickensian, and a lot dirtier and rough around the edges than its Southern neighbor. Its traditional culture is a little more patriarchal (owing somewhat to medieval Thule invasions) but the government's ideals include equality under the law. Visually, they're a lot more tarnish and rivets, with a lot of smoke. <br /> To the immediate west of Mercia are the Faerie Marches, a still wild and untamed region populated by somewhat strange people and even stranger creatures and magic, which separates Mercia from the realms of Elfydd. Elfydd will have at least two or three kingdoms, at least one of which will have a lot of Arthurian overtones. <br /> I only have a vague conception of the rest of the island. As far as &quot;England&quot; goes, Cornwall and the rest of the southwest are probably part of the same kingdom as the southern part of Elfydd/Wales (Monmouth and Glamorgan). Yorkshire and the Northeast, along with the north part of the Northwest, are probably the fourth kingdom. <br /> Beyond that is the lands of Caledonia to the North. It will have at least four or five kingdoms. And werewolves. <br /> <br /> And beyond Albion are the various kingdoms/nations of Hibernia, Gaule, Alamannia, Thule and Hesperia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T21:00:46-07:00","id":1382054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1378946-onyx-path-should-do-a-steampunk-game?p=1380398#post1380398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice, Steampunk is a meaningless word thrown around by a comfortable majority looking for excuse to swageer in the attire and thoughts of a overly romanticized time while still feeling like they're sticking it to their parents.<br /> <br /> I'm quite done with that and want my punk fiction to <i>actually be punk</i>. Not the mayopunk I've been seeing churned out in the last decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah everything you seem to despise is pretty much what I meant by &quot;steampunk&quot;, except for the stick it to your parents part (what does that have to do with sticking to your parents?) . I mean steampunk the way us plebs mean it. Just a stylistic fantsy genre. I couldn't care less about the punk aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 04-17-2020, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"htt